      "writtenOn": "2025-06-16T16:02:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this change will cause a brownout, as during PDC negotiation of new RDO reduces the voltage/power to a safe limit that may not be enough to power the board. @alevkoy@chromium.org @keithshort@chromium.org, can you please confirm?",
      "revId": "e289ff11ebc6eb27e5919e7c0a162ecc389149f7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3411cf51_8e7ea0a0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-16T17:56:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. This _should_ result in the PDC reducing current draw to ~500 mA for ~500 ms. If it doesn\u0027t, that\u0027s probably a PD compliance bug on the part of the PDC.\n\nNote that this spec requirement on PDC behavior only applies for voltage transitions. The PDC _may_ legally renegotiate from 5V/3A to 5V/5A without dropping current draw, if that\u0027s an option. Whether the PDC actually does this probably depends on the PDC.",
      "parentUuid": "7e844669_15a4b294",
      "revId": "e289ff11ebc6eb27e5919e7c0a162ecc389149f7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66b2d92f_6434145f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-18T15:12:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also don\u0027t think this should be under a Kconfig flag.  Our set RDO logic should support battery less systems, as well as missing battery systems consistently.",
      "parentUuid": "3411cf51_8e7ea0a0",
      "revId": "e289ff11ebc6eb27e5919e7c0a162ecc389149f7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3c0cc48_7ff27591",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3387694
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-20T07:23:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because for proto board we might not connect battery always.\nAnd we need adapter can provide over than 5V3A.\nWe will use this as workaround for support no battery system.",
      "parentUuid": "3411cf51_8e7ea0a0",
      "revId": "e289ff11ebc6eb27e5919e7c0a162ecc389149f7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
